 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "hook1",
   "text": "Lesson sixty-seven. Runway crossings. Your sat-nav says: turn left.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "id": "hook2",
   "text": "On the left, there is a runway. And a plane is coming in to land. What is the correct procedure?",
   "gap": 0.7
  },
  {
   "id": "wrong1",
   "text": "A common mistake: drivers trust the sat-nav, and turn onto the runway.",
   "gap": 0.35
  },
  {
   "id": "wrong2",
   "text": "The plane is now directly behind you. Landing speed: two hundred and fifty kilometres per hour.",
   "gap": 0.35
  },
  {
   "id": "wrong3",
   "text": "At this speed, air traffic control treats your car as an aircraft. You are cleared for take-off. Your car now has a flight number.",
   "gap": 0.7
  },
  {
   "id": "wrong4",
   "text": "Exam failed.",
   "gap": 1.1
  },
  {
   "id": "right1",
   "text": "Here's how you do it properly.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "id": "right2",
   "text": "Stop at the yellow holding line. Wait for the plane to land.",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "id": "right3",
   "text": "Switch on your hazard lights, and wait for the follow-me car.",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "id": "right4",
   "text": "It will guide you safely across the runway. Stay close behind it.",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "id": "right5",
   "text": "And give the pilot a friendly wave. Pilots appreciate this.",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "id": "right6",
   "text": "The pilot flashes the landing lights. That means: thank you.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "id": "right7",
   "text": "Exam passed.",
   "gap": 1.2
  },
  {
   "id": "outro",
   "text": "Next lesson: the crash barrier comes alive. Follow, so you don't miss it.",
   "gap": 1.0
  }
 ],
